//! exported, and both are long runs of magic numbers that no reviewer can
//! check by eye. The probe builds a block whose only varying field is the
//! index into the table and reads the table entry off the decoded output, so
//! a transcription error is impossible by construction. Regenerate with:
//!
//! ```sh
//! cc -O2 -I/opt/homebrew/include scripts/ggml_tables.c \
//!    -L/opt/homebrew/lib -lggml-base -o /tmp/ggml_tables && /tmp/ggml_tables
//! ```
//!
//! "Impossible by construction" is only true if the probe's own scale is 1.0,
//! and getting that wrong is silent: a first run of the grid probe left
//! `db` at 1.5 and dumped a table uniformly 1.5x too large, which decodes to
//! correctly-signed, correctly-ordered, wrong weights. The generator now
//! pins the scale by ratio before printing a row. Do not remove that check.
//!
//! There is deliberately no third table. ggml's `ksigns_iq2xs[128]` is
//! `i | (popcount(i) & 1) << 7` -- the eighth sign is a parity bit over the
//! seven stored ones -- which the generator CHECKS for all 128 indices rather
//! than dumping, since a computed byte cannot go stale but a claim about one
//! can. [`crate::quant_gguf_iq::iq3xxs_signs`] is that expression.

